These examples are taken from the test suite of MINKSUM1.8
(https://sites.google.com/site/christopheweibel/research/minksum).

On example naming:

* samp1_1-2.ext
  this is example "samp1", containing two arguments (1-2);
 both are provided using V-representation (.ext)

* samp1_1-2_res.ext
  this is the expected result for example "samp1"; it is provided in case
  the user would like to semantically check the computed result by using
  pplite_lcdd option --check=FILE.
  (Note: option --check is NOT used when running `make check'; we opt for
   a syntactic check, comparing the md5 hash of the output.)
